1.0.4-snapshot
  The AlifeCompanions name, the modded exes check and fixed teleport messages
    Standalone Companions is now AlifeCompanions, in the MCM, the messages and a separate alifecompanions.log.
    The load check now stops the game with a message when the modded exes are missing or too old, and when xlibs is older than 1.5.1.
    Other things you will notice. Teleport messages name the companion, the MCM shows a banner and the live version, and the log names the mod, xlibs and exe versions.

  - Changed the mod name to AlifeCompanions in the MCM and the messages. It logs to a separate alifecompanions.log.
  - Added the modded exes check. The game stops at load with a message when it finds neither demonized 20250908 or newer nor AOEngine.
  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.5.1.
  - Added a banner and the mod version to the General page, and the mod, xlibs and exe versions to the log at startup.
  - Fixed the Go to Anna and Go to Mila messages, which showed {name} in place of her name on the same map and when she could not be found.
  - Fixed Enable, Auto-Spawn and Enable Debug Logging, which had no effect. A companion you switch off or take off auto-spawn no longer spawns.
  - Fixed the auto-spawn timer in modpacks that replace the vanilla timer queue, such as demonized time events.

1.0.3
  An xlibs 1.2.3 floor, with newer xlibs accepted
    From this release the load check accepts xlibs 1.2.3 or any newer compatible version, where it used to ask for 1.2.1 exactly.

  - Changed the xlibs check to accept 1.2.3 or any newer compatible version. It used to stop the game on any version but 1.2.1.

1.0.2
  The xlibs 1.2.1 requirement
    This release runs on xlibs 1.2.1, and the load check asks for that exact version.

  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.2.1.

1.0.1
  An exact xlibs version check
    The load check now matches the xlibs version exactly, where it used to compare the version as text.

  - Fixed the xlibs check comparing versions as text. It now asks for the exact version.

1.0.0
  Anna and Mila, recruited by dialog, with permadeath and teleport
    The first release adds 2 companions you recruit by talking to them, and a companion who dies stays dead.
    Each companion has an MCM page to switch her on, spawn her on load, teleport her to you or you to her, and reset her death.

  - Added Anna, a Duty sniper at the Rostok Bar, who joins you once you have enough Duty goodwill or join Duty.
  - Added Mila, a mercenary at Dead City, who joins you for a fee.
  - Added permadeath. A companion who dies stays dead, and the MCM can reset her death for testing.
  - Added teleport. Teleport to Me brings the companion to you, and Go to her takes you to her, across maps too.
  - Added an xlibs check at load.
